# International > Number Format (dialog 17): a blank 1000 separator, 3 decimal digits, no leading
# zero, OK, then OK in International (tab from Change... to OK) - WIN.INI [intl] is written, the
# blank as " ". Same keys as arch311-ref/scn/intl-number.scn after opening. Run as intl.w16
# (ARCH311_REF_INI=1, ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24", applet International).
# The first frame keeps the caret: 3.11's 1-px caret shows in its selected separator.
# regress: ARCH311_REF_INI=1 ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24" sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" International
# compare: intl-number/02.png 01-open.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-number/03.png 02-number.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-number/04.png 03-changed.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-number/05.png 04-sample.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI intl sThousand=" "
# ini: WIN.INI intl sDecimal=.
# ini: WIN.INI intl iDigits=3
# ini: WIN.INI intl iLzero=0
sleep 900
shot shots/01-open.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 600
shotcaret shots/02-number.png
key space
key tab
key tab
type 3
key tab
key left
sleep 300
shot shots/03-changed.png
key enter
sleep 500
shot shots/04-sample.png
key tab
key enter
sleep 400
quit
